            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ′
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi q
                    %mo ′
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p \circ q)' = (p' \circ q) \cdot q'.
            %p
          %p
            See
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+rule#FormalAlgebra"} here
            for a conceptual proof, using the universal property of adic completion.
          %p
            Relatedly but in a slightly different direction, we can consider differentiation in coalgebraic terms. Suppose the commutative ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
